 ## Background
-The method is based on the parametric octree traversal algorithm proposed by Revelles et al. for the CPU [S1], reformulated and simplified for GPU execution by Forest et al. [S1]. It leverages the Lefebvre et al. GPU-based algorithm for efficient octree cell access [S1], though it differs in solving the ray-traversal specifically. It is used for real-time hierarchical binary-scene voxelization and ray-traced soft shadows [S1].
+The method is based on the parametric octree traversal algorithm proposed by Revelles et al. for the CPU [S1], reformulated and simplified for GPU execution by Forest et al. [S1]. It leverages the Lefebvre et al. GPU-based algorithm for efficient octree cell access [Lefebvre et al. 05], though it explicitly solves the ray-traversal problem which Lefebvre's technique does not [S1]. It is used for real-time hierarchical binary-scene voxelization and ray-traced soft shadows [S1].
 
